close_reason: "Exact OpenAPI operation execution, validation, privacy guards, schemas, docs, PM graph, and layered acceptance delivered for 2026.7.31."
body: "## Context\nOfficial stable 4.x and current main heads remain unchanged and all 181 declared operations are mapped, but agents cannot inspect or execute an exact operation ID through one uniform contract-driven surface.\n\n## Delivery\n- Add `monica api inspect|get|mutate` over both bundled editions.\n- Validate operation identity, method class, path/query inputs, request bodies, content type, and mutation confirmation before dispatch.\n- Keep mutations behind both `--confirm` and the global read-only guard.\n- Integrate deterministic outputs, help, docs, agent contracts, read-only acceptance, current PM/changelog tooling, and release gates.\n\n## Safety\nLive validation uses only GET operations with `readOnlyMode=true`. Credentials, identifiers, response bodies, and private topology stay in `~/.monica-cli` and never enter Git, PM, logs, or GitHub."
